  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep eggplant: Check your avocado is ripe before starting this recipe (see Kitchen hack). Preheat the grill to high. Line an oven tray with foil, then grease the foil. Cut the eggplant into 2cm-thick rounds.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2116324/photos/large/290071_1-8158fcf9a89688f5d7cbbb3a5f56de86.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make sesame dressing: Put 1 tsp sugar and 2 tsp boiling water in a large bowl and stir until the sugar dissolves. Add the sesame seeds, 1 tbs soy sauce and 1 tsp white vinegar and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2116325/photos/large/290071_2-850f5fbc8cd6dd7c50e02cbe4a9f9753.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grill eggplant and tofu: Put the eggplant and tofu on the lined tray and grill for 9 mins or until golden. Turn and grill for a further 9 mins or until golden and the eggplant is tender. Drizzle the eggplant and tofu with half the sesame dressing.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2116326/photos/large/290071_3-2c58eb29d3998115e8ac9b804a063ea5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make avo slaw: Meanwhile, thinly slice the cabbage with a sharp knife or mandoline. Thinly slice the avocado. Thinly slice the spring onion. Add the cabbage to the remaining sesame dressing and toss to coat. Add the avocado and gently toss to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2116327/photos/large/290071_4-67748553711fa9d215a8955141720ff9.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the avo slaw among plates. Stack the eggplant and tofu on the plates, drizzle with 2 tbs vegan mayonnaise and spoon over any tray juices. Scatter with the spring onion and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2116328/photos/large/290071_5-5ee6b0c70f3ef80250ea13bfc891742f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen hack: To speed up the ripening process, put the avocado in a paper bag and loosely close, then leave on the kitchen bench for a day or two. Add a banana to the bag to make the avocado ripen faster.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2116329/photos/large/290071_6-6008943387a372362a097cc2b5e7fe2e.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
